{"number": 161, "text": "               not      +  any                 none\n\n\n                                                                The parking lot is empty.\n                                                                There aren't any    Sache    parking}\n                 uP                                             There are no cars   in the parking\n                                                                How  many cars are there in the parking lot?\n                                                                None.\n\n\n               not (-n’t) + any\n                    ©. There aren’t any cars in the parking lot.\n                    ©) Tracey and Jeff don’t have any children.\n                       You can have some coffee, but | don’t want any.\n                no + noun (no cars / no garage, etc.) = not any...or nota...\n                    ©. There are no cars in the parking lot. (= there aren’t any cars)\n                    ©           no coffee. (= we don’t have any coffee)\n                    ©   tt’sanice house, but there’s no garage. (= there isn’t a garage)\n                We use no... especially after have/has and there is/are.\n                negative verb + any = affirmative verb + no\n                    ©.  They don’t have any children. or They have no children.\n                        (not They don't have no children)\n                    ©.  There isn’t any sugar in your coffee. or There’s no sugar in your coffee.\n\n\n                Use no + noun (no money / no children, etc.):\n                        We have no money.\n                    ©)  Everything was OK. There were no problems.\n                Use none alone (without a noun):\n                    ©.  “How  much money  do you have?”  “None.” (= no money)\n                        “Were there any problems?” “No, none.” (= no problems)\n ES             none and no one\n                        = 0 (zero)\n                 no one = nobody\n\n                None  is an answer for How much? / How many? (things or people):\n                    ©   a: How  much  money do you have?\n                        B: None. (= no money)\n                    ©   A: How  many  people did you meet?\n                        B: None. (= no people)\n                 No one is an answer for\n                     ©  a          you meet?                                                               op\n                        B: Noone.  (or Nobody.)\n\n                                                                                                          %\n\n\n                             Unit 41  some and any  Unit 74  anybody/nobody/nothing  etc.  Units 76-77", "char_count": 2634, "mean_conf": 81.46, "word_count": 321, "words": [{"text": "How", "x0": 1403, "y0": 559, "x1": 1495, "y1": 592, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "many", "x0": 1509, "y0": 565, "x1": 1616, "y1": 600, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "cars", "x0": 1628, "y0": 564, "x1": 1702, "y1": 590, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "are", "x0": 1715, "y0": 564, "x1": 1772, "y1": 589, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "there", "x0": 1786, "y0": 552, "x1": 1885, "y1": 588, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "in", "x0": 1900, "y0": 552, "x1": 1931, "y1": 586, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "the", "x0": 1947, "y0": 550, "x1": 2010, "y1": 587, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "parking", "x0": 2025, "y0": 549, "x1": 2167, "y1": 595, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "lot?", "x0": 2181, "y0": 548, "x1": 2246, "y1": 585, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "None.", "x0": 1403, "y0": 619, "x1": 1521, "y1": 652, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "not", "x0": 337, "y0": 916, "x1": 410, "y1": 946, "conf": 93, "bold": false}, {"text": "(-n’t)", "x0": 421, "y0": 906, "x1": 527, "y1": 953, "conf": 82, "bold": false}, {"text": "+", "x0": 541, "y0": 917, "x1": 567, "y1": 942, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "any", "x0": 580, "y0": 916, "x1": 655